cus is on formally defining the dimensions and border components of the rectangles.\n\n\n**Clarifying Enclosure Conditions**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the rules for region filling. My main question is: Do all enclosed zero regions get filled, or only rectangular ones? I'm noticing all filled regions are rectangles, which is crucial. I've realized the crucial aspect is NOT about the grid boundaries being walls, because outside zeros don't get filled. The grid boundary only acts like a wall when enclosed by a shape that forms a closed loop, like a \"C\" or \"U\" shape that touches the edge.\n\n\n",
